---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import { CV_URL } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
	title="About | Itziar Morales"
	description="Software Engineering student in Madrid — systems programming, backend, and data engineering. Also games, fantasy novels, and a home server."
>
	<p class="eyebrow">~/about</p>
	<h1>About</h1>

	<p>
		Hi, I'm Itziar &mdash; a Software Engineering student at <a href="https://www.u-tad.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">U-tad</a> (Madrid)
		with a minor in Data Science &amp; AI, graduating in June 2027. I started programming at 18 at
		<a href="https://www.digipen.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DigiPen Bilbao</a>, detoured through
		Computational Mathematics, and landed here with an unusually wide base: C++ and systems, backend
		services, databases of every persuasion, and the Python data/ML stack. The honest self-ratings
		live in <a href="/stack">~/stack</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Work</h2>
	<p>
		I'm a Data Analytics Intern at MGA (remote), on the data-engineering side of a digital
		transformation: relational schemas, years of spreadsheet data migrated into PostgreSQL, and
		Spring Boot services on top. The best part is turning implicit business rules &mdash; the kind
		that live in people's heads and formula cells &mdash; into constraints the database enforces itself.
	</p>

	<h2>Mathematics</h2>
	<p>
		The constant thread: linear algebra for rendering pipelines, kinematics for collision detection,
		discrete maths for graph traversal, statistics for ML. Three years of Computational Mathematics
		turned that instinct into a foundation &mdash; I think about convergence and numerical stability
		as naturally as I think about runtime complexity.
	</p>

	<h2>Off the clock</h2>
	<ul class="icon-list">
		<li><Icon name="lucide:music" class="li-icon" /><span>Vocational degree in music (violoncello), ABRSM Grade 8 in piano and cello &mdash; which once turned into composing the soundtrack for a college game project</span></li>
		<li><Icon name="lucide:terminal" class="li-icon" /><span>Linux daily driver, a self-hosted server, and dotfiles for window managers and Neovim &mdash; the full setup is in <a href="/uses">~/uses</a></span></li>
		<li><Icon name="lucide:gamepad-2" class="li-icon" /><span>Retro and modern games in equal measure, plus a soft spot for good pixel art from the games I've built &mdash; and Python scripts for slicing tilesets, because wrangling assets by hand gets old fast</span></li>
		<li><Icon name="lucide:book-open" class="li-icon" /><span>A lot of fantasy fiction &mdash; tallied with the games in <a href="/log">~/log</a></span></li>
		<li><Icon name="lucide:cpu" class="li-icon" /><span>I build my own PCs (and the family's, and the server's) &mdash; picking parts is half the fun</span></li>
		<li><Icon name="lucide:languages" class="li-icon" /><span>English C2 (Cambridge CPE), native Spanish, intermediate French &mdash; each one a different lens on the world</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p class="closer">
		What I'm up to <em>right now</em> lives in <a href="/now">~/now</a>. There's a
		<a href={CV_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">CV</a> if you want the concise version, and if any
		of this overlaps with something you're building &mdash; or you just have strong opinions about
		fantasy novels or window managers &mdash; <a href="mailto:itzimr97@pm.me">get in touch</a>.
	</p>

	<style>
		.closer {
			margin-top: 2.4em;
		}
	</style>
</PageLayout>
